# Paths excluded from compile-database coverage, one git pathspec per line, `#`
# for a comment.
#
# The compile-database coverage check reads this file. Lint enumerates compile
# commands, so the listed sources are absent from its inputs. Every tracked
# translation unit is either linted or declared absent here with a written
# reason.
#
# List a directory only when some other build owns it, so that its sources are
# absent from this tree's compile database. Linting them would run clang-tidy on
# invented flags, the failure CXX-00.6 is about. Never list code this build
# compiles, which must be linted. A listing is not a suppression: the project
# that owns the sources still compiles them under warnings-as-errors.

# The installed-package consumers (tests/consumer and the sources of the
# declared consumer cases): separate CMake projects configured against an
# installed pico_logging, built by the `consumer` gate. This tree's build never
# references them, so their translation units are in no half of the merged
# compile database.
tests/consumer/*
tests/consumer-level/*

# The Pico SDK measurement rigs, described in examples/bench/measurements.md.
# Standalone CMake project; its sources belong to a separate SDK build.
examples/bench/*
